}
\details{
Starting from an empty set, each iteration:
\enumerate{
\item \strong{Entry}: among the variables not yet selected, takes the one
with the largest partial F. It enters if its p-value is lower
than or equal to \code{slentry}. Otherwise the selection stops.
\item \strong{Removal}: among the selected variables, takes the one with
the smallest partial F. It is removed if its p-value is greater
than \code{slstay}.
}

The selection also stops when every variable is selected or after
\code{max_iter} iterations. \code{slentry} must be lower than or equal to
\code{slstay}, otherwise a variable could enter and leave in a loop.

Variables whose partial F cannot be computed (constant variable,
variable collinear with the selected ones) are ignored.
}
